You can upgrade your scaffolding;
you can upgrade your LLM;
but don’t do them together.

today my poor man solution to this is looping over tikz gen -&gt; png render -&gt; vision model steering -&gt; tikz gen -&gt; ... which is far from perfect: vision can't tell precise pos and this loop consumes quite some tokens so it's not even poor man. i really wish there's a better way
Quoting @TeX64AI
@hxiao @bclavie Root cause: TikZ doesn't auto-route — paths need manual deflection. `bend left/right` for simple curves; `to[out=...,in=...]` with explicit angles for complex graphs. The hard part for AI: non-overlapping layout needs spatial iteration that single-shot generation can't do.

